      "specialAbilities": [
        {
          "name": "Pounce",
          "type": "ex",
          "description": "A yellowtooth can make a full attack when it makes a charge attack.",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Powerful Charge",
          "type": "ex",
          "description": "A yellowtooth, when it makes a charge attack, he also deals double damage with his gore attack and gains a free action to do a trip combat maneuver. On a failed combat maneuver check, the yellowtooth is not tripped in return. This ability works only on creatures of a size equal to or smaller than the yellowtooth.",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Poison",
          "type": "ex",
          "description": "Sting — injury; save Fort DC 20; frequency 1/round for 4 rounds; effect 1d6 non-elemental damage; cure 1 save.",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Throat-Rip",
          "type": "ex",
          "description": "As a full-round action, a yellowtooth can deliver a coup de grace against a helpless opponent. If the victim survives the attack, he must succeed on a Fortitude save (DC 10 + damage dealt) or dies. Opponents killed in this manner cannot be raised, but Arise, Full-Life, or the like can restore the slain creature to life.",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Slightly jaundiced variant of the voretooth. It stalks the Alstor Slough, waiting for its prey to get stuck in the muck, then launching a pack-wide attack. The threat of a yellowtooth ambush has scared many would-be anglers away from Neeglyss Pond in recent years, but the Hunters are hoping to rectify the situation at long last."
    },
